    }

    // TLSv1 client has no certificate
    if( ssl->endpoint  == SSL_IS_SERVER &&
        ssl->minor_ver != SSL_MINOR_VERSION_0 )
    {
        if( ssl->in_hslen   == 7                    &&
            ssl->in_msgtype == SSL_MSG_HANDSHAKE    &&
            ssl->in_msg[0]  == SSL_HS_CERTIFICATE   &&
            memcmp( ssl->in_msg + 4, "\0\0\0", 3 ) == 0 )
        {
            // ...
        }
    }
    ```
    These blocks check for specific patterns indicating an empty client certificate. The `TLSv1` check uses `memcmp( ssl->in_msg + 4, "\0\0\0", 3 )`. This reads 3 bytes starting from `ssl->in_msg + 4`. If `ssl->in_hslen` (which is 7 in this condition) is less than 7, this could be an out-of-bounds read. However, the condition `ssl->in_hslen == 7` prevents this specific out-of-bounds read.

4.  **Message Type and Length Checks:**
    ```c
    if( ssl->in_msgtype != SSL_MSG_HANDSHAKE )
    {
        // ...
    }

    if( ssl->in_msg[0] != SSL_HS_CERTIFICATE || ssl->in_hslen < 10 )
